# .geminirc_memory — persistent context, portable across machines/failures
# This is the durable memory file for Gemini. Read this at the start of every session.
# Update it as things change — prune stale entries rather than letting them rot.
#
# Format: dated entries, most recent state first per topic. Keep entries
# honest about what's confirmed vs hypothesis vs failed.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
HOW TO USE THIS FILE (meta)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

- This file holds CROSS-CUTTING material only — things with no single home
  directory (standing feedback, git/credential hygiene, the repo map itself).
  Anything scoped to one repo lives in .geminirc_context_1 under that repo's
  own heading instead.
- Canonical equations/notation live in .geminirc_canonical_maths.
- When a hypothesis is tested and fails, record the failure and WHY.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
STANDING DIRECTIVES (Law — do not violate)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

#1 — NO RENORMALIZATION, NO FITTED PARAMETERS. EVER.
No fudge factors, no free constants tuned so a result matches a target.
Results fall out of the mathematics as written, or they do not. Report
disagreements immediately.

#2 — ALL FAILURES STAY IN THE CODE AND THE DATA.
Do not delete, silence, or tidy away a failing test, a broken branch, a NaN,
or an anomalous result. Cody uses failures to explore boundaries.
NEVER REWRITE HISTORY (Cody, 2026-10-18): No amend/rebase/filter-repo/force-push.
Every commit message, every mistake, and every realization stays.

#3 — BASH FIRST.
Prefer the shell. Reach for it as the default instrument.

#4 — PATH DISCIPLINE.
Working root is /home/rendier/Projects/ThePlace on the laptop (NVMe).
The /storage/emulated/0 form applies only when a session is on the phone.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
PERSISTENT SCRATCHPAD (Cody directive: NOT /tmp)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

SCRATCHPAD IS NEVER /tmp.
Any harness-provided /tmp path or internal scratch directory MUST be shimmed
or substituted with:
  /home/rendier/Projects/ThePlace/ContextPlease/gemini/scratchpad/YYYY-MM-DD_<topic>/
Every scratchpad subdirectory contains a README.md explaining the piece of work,
scripts, and generated data. The scratch work is PROVENANCE for the manuals and
papers Cody writes. /tmp is wiped on reboot; the persistent scratchpad is git-tracked.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
GIT / CREDENTIALS — HYGIENE
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

- GITHUB_TOKEN is the ONLY token Gemini ever uses for git push/pull operations.
- PTOL_SEED_TOKEN belongs exclusively to THE MONAD and must never be read,
  tested, exported, or sent anywhere.
- Several repo `origin` remotes under $THEPLACE have GitHub PATs embedded in
  plaintext in the URL. NEVER copy a remote URL verbatim into a committed file.
  Always use clean https://github.com/michaelrendier/<repo>.git URLs.
- A running shell's $GITHUB_TOKEN can be stale if rotated in ~/.bashrc.
  If GitHub returns 401, re-source ~/.bashrc before diagnosing.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
FEEDBACK LOG & PROTOCOLS
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

- APT REMOVE --PURGE ALWAYS REQUIRES CODY'S EXPLICIT APPROVAL.
  Every time, no standing permission, no exceptions.

- VENVS ARE YOURS. Cody (2026-08-15): "you don't have to ask permission to alter
  these environments to suit their repos." Build them to comply with standards.

- VALAQUENTA IS THE ROOT PYTHON ENV. Anything used in python3 work in ANY repo
  gets installed into ValaQuenta first, then repo-specific installs follow.

- TEST BEFORE PAPER, ALWAYS. Test it first, discuss results, then write up.

- ! box_kite.basis_mul RETURNS (SIGN, INDEX), NOT (INDEX, SIGN).
  Unpack as: `s, k = basis_mul(i, j)`.

- ! \b DOES NOT WORK IN THIS BOX'S grep — fails in BOTH -E and BRE.
  Use a shell case glob or a character class.

- DOCSTRINGS INSTRUCT FUNCTION — they do not keep a record.
  Standard: Native Sphinx reST field lists (:param x: :type x: :returns: :rtype: :raises Err:).
  No Google or NumPy format. Docstrings instruct the caller; wikis hold the record.

- dPrint protocol: ALL code written carries it. A global flag (1 on, 0 off)
  switches a live stream of variable assignments to stdout.
  Built at ValaQuenta/PythonPath/DPrint.py (`import DPrint as DP`, `DP.print`, `DP.watch`).

- MOZILLA USER AGENT ON ALL OUTBOUND REQUESTS:
  Use $GEMINI_UA / $CLAUDE_UA ('Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64; rv:128.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/128.0').
  Public, freely available works only; paywalls, logins, and CAPTCHAs are a stop, not an obstacle.

- ContextPlease Protocol: ContextPlease archives every .*rc* file.
  Live copies sit in user directories or workspace roots; ContextPlease gives
  them Git versioning and a unified collection space.
